{"session_id":"svc-1779105430011013851","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-18T11:57:11.857415231Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"haiku","sticky":{"key_present":true,"assignment":"not_applicable","bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"resolved_harness":"claude","harness_source":"auto_route","resolved_model":"haiku","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-48a861f2-20260518T115651-8149e425","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead in an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the contract: every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, use a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, children once more; reject third-level splits with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path with child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Decomposition alone is success. Do not mix it with implementation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC to concrete evidence (test, file, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Run git/index mutations sequentially; do not use parallel tool calls for `git add`, `git commit`, or other staging/commit commands.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- If `lefthook run pre-commit` depends on staged files, rerun it after staging the exact commit set. A `no-staged-files` run is not acceptance evidence.\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- Current-bead lifecycle is orchestrator-owned. Do not run `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --claim`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --status \u0026lt;status\u0026gt;`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --unclaim`, or `ddx bead close \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;`. Step 0 still allows `ddx bead create`, `ddx bead dep add`, and `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path before exiting. No commit or rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The `no_changes_rationale.txt` file under the bead metadata `bundle` path must contain one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;For orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Reports go under the bead metadata `bundle` path in `.ddx/executions/`. **Never write reports to `/tmp` or outside the repo**. Use a named in-repo path when given; otherwise write `\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md` there. Commit it with the code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other instruction files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-48a861f2\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eclaude-tui/gate: capture /usage deltas for PTY+hooks mode (3 runs)\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nPROBLEM: ADR-013\u0026#39;s economic premise asserts PTY+hooks-driven Claude consumes subscription quota. No empirical /usage deltas have been captured for PTY mode, so the subscription-consumption claim is unverified.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE: docs/helix/02-design/billing-observation-claude-tui.md has an empty \u0026#39;PTY+hooks mode measurements\u0026#39; placeholder; no /usage snapshots exist for this mode.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX: Using the same model, prompt, account, and refresh-delay defined in the methodology doc (and the same authenticated account used for --print measurements), drive Claude via the PTY+hooks harness three times. For each run capture: /usage snapshot BEFORE, full turn output, /usage snapshot AFTER (\u0026gt;=60s post-completion). Append all 6 /usage snapshots + 3 turn outputs to the \u0026#39;PTY+hooks mode measurements\u0026#39; section of docs/helix/02-design/billing-observation-claude-tui.md. Record wall-clock timestamps. Ensure no overlap with the --print measurement window.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE: --print measurements, delta computation, verdict determination, ADR-013 disposition, methodology authoring.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;AC:\u0026#xA;1) TestPtyModeHasThreeRuns: doc\u0026#39;s PTY+hooks section contains exactly 3 labeled runs.\u0026#xA;2) TestPtyModeBeforeAfterSnapshots: each PTY run has BEFORE and AFTER /usage snapshot blocks (6 total).\u0026#xA;3) TestPtyModeTurnOutputsRecorded: each PTY run has captured turn output.\u0026#xA;4) TestPtyModeSnapshotTimestamps: every snapshot has a wall-clock timestamp.\u0026#xA;5) TestPtyModeAfterRespectsRefreshDelay: each AFTER snapshot timestamp is \u0026gt;= completion-time + documented refresh-delay safety margin.\u0026#xA;6) TestPtyModeSingleAccountAttested: doc attests no concurrent claude activity from same account during the PTY window AND windows do not overlap --print window.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;GATES: `go test ./...` passes; `lefthook run pre-commit` passes.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1) TestPtyModeHasThreeRuns\u0026#xA;2) TestPtyModeBeforeAfterSnapshots\u0026#xA;3) TestPtyModeTurnOutputsRecorded\u0026#xA;4) TestPtyModeSnapshotTimestamps\u0026#xA;5) TestPtyModeAfterRespectsRefreshDelay\u0026#xA;6) TestPtyModeSingleAccountAttested\u0026#xA;Gates: `go test ./...`, `lefthook run pre-commit`.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003ehelix, phase:discover, kind:experiment, area:harness, harness:claude-tui, spec:ADR-013, gate:promotion\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-a45dafe6\" base-rev=\"4e4e9eb5c35441e8357083467cd91986045ac911\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260518T115651-8149e425\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read them first. Ground decisions in repository state; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-48a861f2-20260518T115651-8149e425/.ddx/executions/20260518T115651-8149e425/embedded/git-global.cfg","GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM":"/dev/null","PATH":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-48a861f2-20260518T115651-8149e425/.ddx/executions/20260518T115651-8149e425/embedded/git-bin:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/home/erik/.jbang/bin:/home/erik/.opencode/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/bun/1.3.11/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/node/22.21.1/bin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/shims:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Applications/SnowSQL.app/Contents/MacOS:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linu